  "question": "Which explicit short-path families and critical-value estimates are proved for Erdős #1041, and which of those statements have Lean or Comparator checks?",
  "precis": "The paper gives ordinary proofs of the length-less-than-2 conclusion for monic trinomials z^n+a z^m+b, with 1≤m<n and all roots in the open unit disc. For squarefree monic polynomials, if the least critical-value modulus μ is at most 13/25, there is also such a connector. Without a root-location restriction, the scaled result gives a path shorter than (5/2) μ^(1/n) in {|f|<(25/13)μ}. Separate length-area and critical-value estimates give further control. Exact counterexamples show why these ingredients do not yield the unrestricted connector theorem; Erdős #1041 remains open.",
  "owns": "the problem-specific exposition for Erdős #1041: ordinary all-degree trinomial paths, a sharp critical-value mean, subsidiary Lean and Comparator checks, and exact obstructions that prevent promoting those estimates to a general connector theorem",
  "not_authority_for": "the validity of claims tagged Lean, which belongs to the cited kernel-checked source, or a solution to Erdős #1041, which remains open",
